  "insight": "The VIP appointment videos that welcome every credit situation (ITIN, first-time buyers, business owners) brought the most messages per dollar, led by the Puente Hills and Mazda versions, with the work-truck ad close behind. The Surf City lead form test brought the lowest cost lead forms, so lean into those angles and refresh the weaker Surf City message ad.",
  "insights": {
    "creative": "Every top ad runs the VIP-visit pitch in Spanish. The Puente Hills video, headline 'Sí, ayúdame a conseguir un auto', lists ITIN, self-employed, first-time buyers and all credit types, and led with 593 conversations at $8.62. Mazda's 'Si Si, quiero un auto nuevo' video brought 298 at $9.43; Audi's work-truck ad, 'Necesitas una Troca pa la Chamba?', 293 at $9.33. We recommend testing the truck headline in Puente Hills and Corona, where only the car pitch runs.",
    "doing": "September booked 906 appointments from 7,207 conversations and 1,798 lead forms, against 973 appointments, 7,668 conversations and 1,773 lead forms in August. Cost per conversation rose to $13.61 from $12.84, and cost per lead form eased to $54.57 from $55.53.",
    "look_into": "Audi holds 565 of the 906 booked appointments; the other dealerships' bookings are not in the Valencia system, so they read 0 here. Surf City costs the most per conversation at $21.14 against $13.61 overall, and four September ads were not approved in Meta's review.",
    "next": "We recommend reviewing Surf City's ads and audience first, since it starts conversations at nearly twice the account cost, and giving the September videos launched Sep 22 to 26 a full month before judging them against the older control ads."
  },
